MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and layered heavy sound.",
    "The Sickness follows my interest in Ten Thousand Fists, while Hybrid Theory and Toxicity connect with my interest in heavy riffs, strong rhythms, and memorable hooks."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Marshall Mathers and Get Rich Or Die Tryin' miss what I want now: guitar-driven rock and metal. An intense delivery or explicit lyrics alone does not give me the musical connection I am seeking.",
    "St. Anger and Fallen have elements I enjoy, but heaviness or melody alone is not enough to make them priorities over exploring more Tool and Disturbed today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat aggressive music as broadly interchangeable, even though rap does not satisfy my current interest in heavy guitar riffs.",
    "The list seems to give broad rock and metal appeal more weight than the specific sounds I am most interested in exploring right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interactions with 10.000 Days and Ten Thousand Fists make other albums by Tool and Disturbed especially compelling next steps.",
    "I care about how the music combines intricate rhythms, forceful riffs, and melody; sharing just one of those qualities makes an album plausible without making it a choice for today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my interest in heavy music, but some stretch that interest beyond the guitar-driven sound and specific bands I want to explore now."
}
